Using the sampling property of the Dirac delta function, \[\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}f(t)\,\delta(t-a)\,dt=f(a),\] provided \(a\) lies within the limits of integration. Here, \[f(t)=e^{-2t}, \qquad a=1.\] Since \(1\in[-5,6]\), \[\int_{-5}^{6}e^{-2t}\delta(t-1)\,dt
=e^{-2(1)}
=e^{-2}.\] \[\boxed{\text{(b) }e^{-2}}\]

